    Coding Style matters even if you're coding solo (by yourself), like when asking for help on the forum, hiring freelancer, freelancing, finding a partner and your future self when reading the code after a long time.
    A Good Code Style is a code that is easy to understand, no right or wrong answer, no one true style, but better and worse answers, and mainly readability through consistency.
    The basic elements to consider a Good Code Style are Indentation, Whitescpace, Capitalization, Naming and Comments.
